{"connection_id":"BC-9aabb44eb4656c31cb91","ref":"WLC:Deut.26.10","status":"rejected","reason":"Firstfruits are set before YHWH in worship, but this is produce, not animal or friend-gift; Deut 12:11 covers offerings.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Deut.26.10"],"annotations":[]}
{"connection_id":"BC-057bb7e94f152778d5d2","ref":"WLC:Deut.26.2","status":"rejected","reason":"Fruit basket reaches chosen Name-place, but the commentary's tray holds a personal gift; ritual recipient differs.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Deut.26.2"],"annotations":[]}
{"connection_id":"BC-759f3b718eb559c63653","ref":"WLC:Deut.30.4","status":"rejected","reason":"God gathers far exiles but no road or specific home in verse 4; Ps 107:7 gives both.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Deut.30.4"],"annotations":[]}
{"connection_id":"BC-8fc139b9381044aa6057","ref":"WLC:Deut.30.5","status":"rejected","reason":"Exiles are brought to inherited land, not the sacred house or straight path central here.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Deut.30.5"],"annotations":[]}
{"connection_id":"BC-ecb8ee22e08b36d26f5b","ref":"WLC:Deut.6.13","status":"accepted","reason":"Hebrew taavod is service of God, a supported cognate to Arabic ibada service.","paragraphs":[62],"evidence":["WLC:Deut.6.13","WLC:Exod.3.12"],"annotations":["S001-TEV-SYD-002"]}
{"connection_id":"BC-6eeb25622a2ae86a601e","ref":"WLC:Deut.6.13","status":"accepted","reason":"Service and Name-oath coexist; annotation limits the lexical link to worshipful service.","paragraphs":[62],"evidence":["WLC:Deut.6.13","WLC:Exod.3.12"],"annotations":["S001-TEV-SYD-002"]}
{"connection_id":"BC-b2b3cb1c091df639836a","ref":"WLC:Esth.2.16","status":"rejected","reason":"Esther is taken to royal palace, but verse does not yet call her wife; Gen 24 narrates bridal journey and union.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Esth.2.16"],"annotations":[]}
{"connection_id":"BC-a9c163faf4a3ad04c4d8","ref":"WLC:Esth.2.16","status":"rejected","reason":"Melekh is king, but verse does not connect king-word to marriage-acquisition term of Arabic imlak.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Esth.2.16"],"annotations":[]}
{"connection_id":"BC-93f9b0410a05f9058054","ref":"WLC:Exod.12.13","status":"rejected","reason":"Passover blood is a sign on houses; the commentary's mawsim mark is seasonal, not a protective blood mark.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Exod.12.13"],"annotations":[]}
{"connection_id":"BC-55c69797746ee14f66a1","ref":"WLC:Exod.12.13","status":"rejected","reason":"Marked house is spared in plague, but its occupants are not petitioners under community oath.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Exod.12.13"],"annotations":[]}
{"connection_id":"BC-acc8d5ff4b624a1bba4e","ref":"WLC:Exod.12.27","status":"rejected","reason":"Passover sacrifices protect households in Egypt; animals are chosen per home, not taken to chosen House.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Exod.12.27"],"annotations":[]}
