{"connection_id":"BC-472b40aa5c1e969e7c8e","ref":"WLC:Exod.13.21","status":"rejected","reason":"Cloud and fire lead Israel along way, but this verse names no dwelling endpoint; Exod 15:13,17 does.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Exod.13.21"],"annotations":[]}
{"connection_id":"BC-96f1401a73e0ee37df4c","ref":"WLC:Exod.15.13","status":"accepted","reason":"Redeemed people are led toward holy abode, joined to verse 17 and Ps 43:3.","paragraphs":[64],"evidence":["WLC:Exod.15.13","WLC:Exod.15.17","WLC:Ps.43.3"],"annotations":["S001-TEV-MTF-006"]}
{"connection_id":"BC-313bcd820cedd220096b","ref":"WLC:Exod.15.17","status":"accepted","reason":"God brings and plants people at the place of his dwelling and sanctuary.","paragraphs":[64],"evidence":["WLC:Exod.15.13","WLC:Exod.15.17","WLC:Ps.43.3"],"annotations":["S001-TEV-MTF-006"]}
{"connection_id":"BC-8d2780e61f312a0abcd6","ref":"WLC:Exod.19.4","status":"rejected","reason":"God brings people to himself, not specifically a house; John 14:2-3 combines personal reception with dwelling.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Exod.19.4"],"annotations":[]}
{"connection_id":"BC-02505e288847e9fa39be","ref":"WLC:Exod.20.24","status":"rejected","reason":"Shem occurs at altar, but this verse cannot establish the proposed Arabic ism cognacy or its derivation.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Exod.20.24"],"annotations":[]}
{"connection_id":"BC-c6af587b7fa290f58e93","ref":"WLC:Exod.20.24","status":"rejected","reason":"Altar, flocks, Name and blessing coexist, but permission at every named place differs from Deut 12's chosen destination.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Exod.20.24"],"annotations":[]}
{"connection_id":"BC-bc631de54efe1eb24c4b","ref":"WLC:Exod.21.13","status":"rejected","reason":"God appoints a place for accidental killer to flee, but no gate reception or settled home is narrated.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Exod.21.13"],"annotations":[]}
{"connection_id":"BC-967754e1aff3fc8e464b","ref":"WLC:Exod.21.13","status":"rejected","reason":"Flight to appointed place is explicit but Josh 20:4 spells out communal admission; Deut 23:16-17 adds residence.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Exod.21.13"],"annotations":[]}
{"connection_id":"BC-80eec52a053511156a44","ref":"WLC:Exod.21.14","status":"accepted","reason":"Premeditated murderer must be taken even from altar; annotation states the limit of sacred protection.","paragraphs":[63],"evidence":["WLC:Deut.23.16","WLC:Deut.23.17","WLC:Josh.9.15","WLC:Josh.9.19","WLC:Exod.21.14"],"annotations":["S001-TEV-MTF-005"]}
{"connection_id":"BC-a5979a2d592745af0f8c","ref":"WLC:Exod.21.14","status":"accepted","reason":"Altar asylum is legally limited for deliberate murder, a concrete counterpoint to inviolability image.","paragraphs":[63],"evidence":["WLC:Deut.23.16","WLC:Deut.23.17","WLC:Josh.9.15","WLC:Josh.9.19","WLC:Exod.21.14"],"annotations":["S001-TEV-MTF-005"]}
{"connection_id":"BC-bf91ab095bd637457ae2","ref":"WLC:Exod.23.15","status":"rejected","reason":"Appointed feast and no empty hands are present, repeating the seasonal-gift point annotated from Lev 23:2 and Deut 16:16.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Exod.23.15"],"annotations":[]}
{"connection_id":"BC-823e33e0876729dd7c40","ref":"WLC:Exod.23.20","status":"rejected","reason":"Angel guards route to prepared place, but that place is not named as a house; Ps 43:3 is explicit.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Exod.23.20"],"annotations":[]}
{"connection_id":"BC-a1269aa9ed5ead5ad9e7","ref":"WLC:Exod.3.12","status":"accepted","reason":"Inflected Hebrew taavdun is from service root and directs worship to God at mountain.","paragraphs":[62],"evidence":["WLC:Deut.6.13","WLC:Exod.3.12"],"annotations":["S001-TEV-SYD-002"]}
{"connection_id":"BC-3cba5a73435e4e6aff24","ref":"WLC:Exod.34.24","status":"rejected","reason":"Promise protects land during festivals, not the pilgrims as asylum seekers or the transported animal.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Exod.34.24"],"annotations":[]}
{"connection_id":"BC-299e832fefc2ff814ecf","ref":"WLC:Exod.34.26","status":"rejected","reason":"Firstfruits are brought to God's house, but produce is not the hedy animal; Deut 12:11 has name and offerings.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Exod.34.26"],"annotations":[]}
